It does not follow this particular implementation, mainly because I did not become aware of the parameterization until a good chunk of the package was already written. The nominal, gpcm (and pcm), and 2PL are therefore all separate implementations and classes rather than estimated with particular T matrices; which isn't a problem, it's just not as elegant as defining a T matrix for each special case of the nominal model.

